<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What the launcher needs to know before it will offer this widget in the picker.

    `updatePeriodMillis` is 0 on purpose. Android floors it at 30 minutes, which is far too slow to
    be the mechanism behind a ± press and far too often to be worth waking the device for otherwise.
    Every repaint this widget does is pushed instead: by the app after it writes a snapshot
    (HabitsWidgetPlugin.refresh), by the provider itself after a press, and by ACTION_DATE_CHANGED
    at midnight — see the intent-filter in AndroidManifest.xml. Nothing is left to a poll.

    `previewLayout` deliberately points at a layout of its own rather than at the real one. The real
    one is a title above an *empty* container — its rows only exist once the provider has a snapshot
    to build them from, and nothing runs a provider to render a picker entry — so pointing this at
    it produced a correct, working, entirely blank card. See widget_habits_preview.xml.

    `previewImage` is the pre-31 fallback and is deliberately not set: it would have to be a raster,
    which cannot follow the launcher's dark mode and goes stale the moment a colour changes. Older
    launchers show the app icon instead, which is honest rather than wrong.

    The minimum size is about three habits. `resizeMode` matters more than the minimum here: a habits
    list is exactly the kind of thing people want to stretch to the height of their actual list, and
    the layout has no fixed row count to fight it.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_habits"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_habits_preview"
    android:description="@string/widget_habits_description"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
